  "notes": [
    "RVS933: Included as follow_up because the paper records a prior hypervelocity-catalogue entry (T:p5-b3); this paper confirms its high radial velocity but does not itself establish Galactic unbound status. RVS1281: Similarly included from the prior hypervelocity catalogue (T:p5-b7); its proposed LRK2022 moving-group membership is not treated here as a Galactic-unbound determination. The sample-wide |Vr| > 500 km/s selection (T:p2-b2) and the confirmation of high radial velocities (T:p7-b6) do not by themselves establish Galactic unbound candidacy, so no candidates_found entries were made.",
    "RVS933: Table 2 (T:p11-b0) reports J2000 sexagesimal coordinates, Gaia DR3 radial velocity, and its uncertainty for RVS933. No parallax, distance, proper motion, galactocentric radius, Galactic rest-frame velocity, or bound/unbound probability is reported for this star in the supplied material.",
    "RVS1281: Table 2 (T:p11-b0) gives the RVS1281 declination as “-50 08 56.77” with spaces rather than colons; I retained the reported spacing and interpreted it as the J2000 declination -50:08:56.77. No numerical parallax, distance, proper motions, galactocentric radius, rest-frame speed, or bound/unbound probability is reported for RVS1281."
  ]
